          <caption>
            <p>Hypertrophic Scar Formation. This image shows a hypertrophic scar. This type of&#x000a0;scar, which forms after the wound has closed, is characterized by raised, red tissue that remains confined to the wound boundaries. This complication arises from excessive collagen production. Courtesy of DermNet NZ,&#x000a0;https://dermnetnz.org/topics/risks-and-complications-of-skin-surgery, accessed 06/13/24</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Screenshot__2024-06-13__at__6.52.58__PM" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
